  "name": "Question 6",
  "problem": "If ${2}^{5},{2}^{7},$ and ${2}^{9}$ are elements of $B$, but ${3}^{4}$ and ${5}^{0}$ are not, then which of the following is true?",
  "worked_solution": "If $a$ is an element of $S,$ we write $a\\in S.$ Otherwise, if $a$ is *not* an element of $S,$ we write $a\\notin S.$\n\n- Since ${2}^{5},{2}^{7},$ and ${2}^{9}$ are elements of $B,$ we write ${2}^{5},{2}^{7},{2}^{9}\\in B.$\n\n- Since ${3}^{4}$ and ${5}^{0}$ are *not* elements of $B,$ we write ${3}^{4},{5}^{0}\\notin B.$\n\nAll together, we have the following statement:\n\n$\\,$  ${2}^{5},{2}^{7},{2}^{9}\\in B$ and ${3}^{4},{5}^{0}\\notin B$",
